            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration can be used efficiently for pathological diagnosis of bronchial walls and surrounding structures. Patients with hemoptysis, fistulas or foreign-body-aspiration can be treated bronchoscopically, but remain a challenge for the hospital team involved.</AbstractText>
